-- help.txt --
AIGW  aigw check
────────────────────────────────────────
  Check the enabled clients, or the named ones, enabled or not; <client> is claude, claude-desktop, codex, or hermes.
  Each depth runs the ones before it: local checks the configuration, the Token's presence, the
  client files and the environment without a request; endpoint sends one authenticated request
  that names no model; model, the default, sends one bounded inference request, which may use
  quota; client runs a real client session, which may use more. A client stops at its first
  failed depth, and a depth that a client cannot run is skipped with the reason.

Usage
  aigw check [client...] [flags]

Examples
  aigw check
  aigw check claude --depth client
  aigw check --depth local --verbose

Options
      --depth string   How far to check: local, endpoint, model or client (default model)
  -h, --help           help for check
      --json           Write one JSON document, which carries every local check
      --model string   Try this provider/model with the one named client, without selecting it
      --token-stdin    Read a one-time Token for --model from standard input, at the endpoint or model depth; it is neither read from nor written to the store
      --verbose        Print every local check
-- empty.txt --
AIGW  Action required
────────────────────────────────────────

Problem
  AIGW is not set up

Evidence
  No provider has been added.

Impact
  No client was checked.

Fix
  aigw setup
